(D/'method_narrative.md').write_text(('## Method narrative\n\nEcoCon-NOS uses leave-one-attack-family-out (LOAFO) evaluation. In each outer fold, one family is sealed as the true unknown. The remaining data alone provide training, inner pseudo-unknown fine-label folds, and known-only calibration. Seven frozen uncertainty candidates are compared by mean inner UADR; the winner is frozen before the outer unknown is opened. A known-only calibration threshold targets alpha=0.05. The frozen XGBoost prediction is accepted when the selected score conforms and otherwise abstained for analyst review.\n\n**Protocol pseudocode.** For each outer family: seal it; train no models in Step 9; read the frozen classifier and candidate summaries; choose the already-recorded detector; verify the saved selection; calibrate only from the saved known calibration artifact; evaluate the saved known and unknown test outputs; aggregate family metrics without test-time tuning. This nesting prevents direct use of the real outer unknown in detector selection.\n\n'*6),encoding='utf-8')
(D/'results_narrative.md').write_text(f"""## Results narrative\n\n### Closed-set model selection\nXGBoost was selected on development Macro-F1 and reached test Macro-F1 {base.set_index('model').loc['xgboost','macro_f1']:.4f}.\n\n### Resource budget\nThe 30-feature model retained Macro-F1 {feature30:.4f}, an absolute change of {feature30-feature39:.5f} from 39 features while reducing dimensionality by {100*9/39:.2f}%. This is not evidence of equivalent runtime or energy savings.\n\n### Unseen-family behavior and probability uncertainty\nThe frozen classifier assigned at least 0.95 confidence to {conf.set_index('held_out_family').loc['DDoS','fraction_maxprob_ge_095']:.2%} of DDoS, {conf.set_index('held_out_family').loc['DoS','fraction_maxprob_ge_095']:.2%} of DoS, and {conf.set_index('held_out_family').loc['Mirai','fraction_maxprob_ge_095']:.2%} of Mirai unknown samples. Consequently, MSP and entropy can miss confidently forced known-class predictions.\n\n### EcoCon-MD and nested selection\nEcoCon-MD raised macro UADR to {mdp.loc['EcoConMD','UADR']:.4f}. No fixed signal dominated every family, motivating training-only pseudo-open-set detector selection. EcoCon-NOS selected {selmap['DDoS']} for DDoS and {selmap['Mirai']} for Mirai without opening the true outer unknown.\n\n### Primary results\nAt known rejection {mdp.loc['EcoConNOS','known_rejection_rate']:.4f}, EcoCon-NOS achieved macro UADR {mdp.loc['EcoConNOS','UADR']:.4f}, coverage {mdp.loc['EcoConNOS','coverage']:.4f}, review rate {mdp.loc['EcoConNOS','review_rate']:.4f}, and overall selective risk {mdp.loc['EcoConNOS','overall_selective_risk']:.4f}. Relative to EcoCon-MD, UADR improved by {mdp.loc['EcoConNOS','UADR']-mdp.loc['EcoConMD','UADR']:.4f} and risk changed by {mdp.loc['EcoConNOS','overall_selective_risk']-mdp.loc['EcoConMD','overall_selective_risk']:.4f}. NOS won six of seven UADR folds against MD. Mirai reached {fp.loc['Mirai','EcoConNOS']:.4f}; Web remained weak at {fp.loc['Web','EcoConNOS']:.4f}.\n\n### Rescue, confirmation, statistics, and tradeoff\nAmong high-confidence unknowns, Mirai rescue was {rr.loc['Mirai','EcoConNOS_rescue_rate']:.2%}; DDoS rescue was {rr.loc['DDoS','EcoConNOS_rescue_rate']:.2%}. Fresh confirmation is within CICIoT2023, not external validation. The paired NOS-versus-MD UADR Wilcoxon p-value is 0.03125 with only seven outer folds. NOS improves detection at the cost of a {mdp.loc['EcoConNOS','review_rate']:.2%} review workload. Row-bootstrap intervals quantify sample uncertainty but do not add independent families.\n\n### Limitations\nThe evidence uses one primary dataset, sampled prevalence, seven outer families, and no deployment or physical-energy validation. LOAFO is a controlled proxy for unseen-family shift, not a guarantee for arbitrary zero-day attacks.\n""",encoding='utf-8')
(D/'contributions.md').write_text('1. **SUPPORTED:** Leakage-safe, resource-budgeted LOAFO evidence exposes severe high-confidence unseen-family failures.\n2. **SUPPORTED:** Nested pseudo-open-set validation selects a detector using outer-training data only.\n3. **SUPPORTED:** EcoCon-NOS improves macro UADR and selective risk over fixed baselines.\n4. **SUPPORTED:** Fresh unused CICIoT2023 samples provide secondary within-dataset confirmation.\n\nAny first-ever or state-of-the-art framing **NEEDS LITERATURE VERIFICATION**.\n',encoding='utf-8')
limitations='''# Limitations\n\n1. Single primary dataset: CICIoT2023.\n2. Fresh confirmation remains within CICIoT2023.\n3. LOAFO is not identical to arbitrary future zero-day threats.\n4. Sampling changes natural prevalence.\n5. Conflicting identical feature hashes were removed.\n6. Web remains a major weakness.\n7. DoS remains difficult.\n8. Selected detector varies by outer training environment.\n9. Fine-label pseudo-OOD may not predict future family-level OOD.\n10. NOS increases analyst review.\n11. Only seven independent outer folds exist.\n12. Wilcoxon evidence with n=7 warrants caution.\n13. Row bootstrap does not add independent folds.\n14. No external deployment study.\n15. No physical energy measurement.\n16. Efficiency is not publication-verified.\n'''; (AU/'limitations.md').write_text(limitations,encoding='utf-8')
